local _, ns = ...
ns.chapters = {
  [529] = {
    start = { title = "In the Light", { "Come in, come in! No, stand there, in the light, where I can see you properly." }, { "You have the look of someone who can swing a weapon and has not yet been told what for. That is where I come in. The Dawn has one enemy, the dead, and no interest at all in which of the living you came from. Take our commission. What the Scourge carries on it is of great interest to me, and then we shall know what you are." }, { "One more thing. Everything in this world that is pushed too far becomes its own enemy. Courage. Faith. The Light itself. Remember that. I shall ask you about it later." } },
    friendly = { title = "Insignia", { "You have been about the Plaguelands long enough now that we may talk as colleagues." }, { "Do you know what they carry, the dead? Insignia. The Scourge is an army, and an army has ranks, even when its soldiers are dead. The common stones mark its rank and file. The rarer mark its elite. The rarest belong to its masters, the creatures that give the orders, and they are worth a great deal more than the rest. I keep the count. Some nights it is the only proof I have that we are winning." }, { "Every set brought to me earns a token. Somewhere in the Plaguelands, a thing that once took orders has stopped taking them. I find that very satisfying. I suspect that says something about me, and I have no intention of finding out what." } },
    honored = { title = "A Spine of Iron", { "I promised to ask you about extremes. Here is my question. What do you call a man who fights the Scourge, prays to the Light, and kills the innocent because he will not trouble to tell them from the guilty? The Scarlet Crusade calls him a crusader. I call him a blasphemer!" }, { "They hold part of Stratholme. Inside it, a man named Galford keeps their archive, years of what they are pleased to call intelligence." }, { "I want it burned. I want him dead. Tell me that is unreasonable. Go on.", before = 5251 }, { "You burned it for me, and that night I slept better than I have in years. Tell me that was unreasonable. Go on.", after = 5251 }, { "You see, we of the Dawn are tolerant. Tolerance is not softness. It needs a spine of iron, or the first fanatic to come along will bend it double. I have a spine of iron." } },
    revered = { title = "Those Who Come Back", { "You will have noticed that I am always here when you return. I send. That is what I do. I send people like you into Stratholme and the dead fields, and I wait at Light's Hope and count what comes back, the stones and the people. The stones always come back." }, { "So I keep two counts. The stones go in the ledger, where the quartermasters can see them. The other count I keep nowhere at all, and I could recite every line of it to you." }, { "You will also have noticed that I never call the Scourge's rank and file weak. I learned why from the ones who did not come back." }, { "Naxxramas is up there, Kel'Thuzad's citadel, and the Dawn will send people into it. Some of them will be people I sent somewhere else first." }, { "And you brought me a demon's head out of Stratholme, and I have not yet decided what it means. Those people in red believed they served the Light. They were serving a dreadlord. I called them blasphemers. I should like to know what to call them now.", after = 5262 } },
    aside = { title = "The aside", { "You are still coming back. I have stopped being surprised by it, which, I warn you, is the first step towards depending on it." } },
    exalted = { title = "Champion", { "Champion." }, { "Kneel. No, do not kneel. I am not a king, and you would only get up again with that look on your face." }, { "I have not called anyone that in years. I should like you to understand that I do not use the word loosely, because I do not use anything loosely, as you may have noticed." }, { "I told you once that everything pushed too far becomes its own enemy. I have thought about it a great deal since, which is your fault. I am a man who would burn a library for the Light and call the smoke a sermon. If anyone in this chapel is in danger of becoming what he hates, my friend, it is not you." }, { "That is why I need you. A champion is not someone who agrees with me. A champion is someone I trust to tell me when I have gone too far, and whom I will believe. I have not had one for a long time." }, { "The war is not over. One day the Dawn will go against the master of all this, wherever he sits, and on that day I should like you near me. Not in front. Near." } },
  },
  [576] = {
    start = { title = "The Door", { "I saw you coming up the road. You want the tunnel. Strangers always want the tunnel, because it is shorter than the mountains. It is not yours." }, { "We are the Timbermaw, the last tribe the corruption has not taken. You have met the others. Everyone has, and everyone shoots first now, without stopping to look. So do we." }, { "Grazle will tell you how to change our minds. Grazle tells everyone everything. Do what he asks, and then do it again." }, { "I will be here, at the door. I have one eye. For you, it is enough." } },
    friendly = { title = "The Count", { "From here on, it is counting." }, { "Feathers off the headdresses of the Deadwood, to Nafien at the gate or to Grazle, for those who bring them. They tell me the count whether I ask or not. I do not enjoy it. The Deadwood were our kin before the fel got into Felwood and into them, and a feather does not say which of them it was." }, { "The beads are worse. The Winterfall carried them against foul spirits. You can see how well that went. They wore their wards, the foulness walked in anyway, and now their beads go to Salfa in strangers' bags." }, { "Salfa thinks you are useful, and Salfa is seldom wrong. I still watch you." } },
    honored = { title = "What Few Have Asked", { "You have walked the hold so often now that the guards no longer reach for anything when you pass. So here is something, and you may do with it whatever your kind does with things it is told." }, { "The night elves took our help once, against the demons, and many of them took it holding their noses. Some of them have not stopped. Ask the Sentinels, on a day they feel honest." }, { "The Winterfall were our friends, and not long ago. Then their high chief began to want things nobody understood, and his tribe turned on everyone near it, us with the rest. Since then we keep to ourselves. We learned that much." }, { "Your people write their history down. We do not. And what we hold dearest, you have walked through a hundred times without seeing. Not yet." } },
    revered = { title = "Said Once", { "I will say this once, and you will not repeat it to Grazle." }, { "We cannot hold this place alone. Salfa tells strangers so, because Salfa is honest to a fault. I say it to you because you are not a stranger any more, which I did not expect to be saying this year. If the Winterfall and the Deadwood came at us from two sides at once, we would need every friend we have, and there are not many." }, { "Your kings have sent word to this hold before. The dwarf king under his mountain. The warchief of the orcs, in Durotar. They wanted to talk. There was no peace. I could give you the reasons, but you would not like them, and most of them would be about your people." }, { "You are Revered among us. Here the word means something plainer than it does among you. It means that if you fell at the door, someone would come out for you. It would be me. I would complain the whole way." } },
    aside = { title = "The aside", { "Still here. Still counting. Salfa says you are halfway to something. Salfa likes saying things like that. When you have arrived, you will hear it from me." } },
    exalted = { title = "Walk Slower", { "Walk slower through the hold from now on. You will, once you know why." }, { "You think this place is a road. A good road, out of the snow, with furbolgs in it who have learned not to shoot you. It was never a road. The hold was made for Ursoc and Ursol, the twin bears we honor, and every tunnel you have hurried through to save yourself a mountain is part of it. We let those we trust walk through a holy place. Most of them never knew what it was. Now you do." }, { "You will ask about the eye. Everyone who gets this far asks about the eye. No." }, { "I was the last in this hold to trust you, and I would like that remembered, because I was right to be slow. Trust that comes easily leaves the same way. Mine came the slow way, and it is not going anywhere." }, { "There is one more thing, and we do not give it to many. In a bad hour, far from here, one of our ancestors will come and stand with you, and mend you while it fights. Not for small hours. They are old, and they are ours, and they come as a favor to me.", after = 8481 } },
  },
  [59] = {
    start = { title = "Insects", { "An insect. At my table. Speaking to me." }, { "We have no business with insects, and I have no patience for them. You have nothing I want, you know nothing I need, and you are blocking my view of the door. The Brotherhood walked out on the emperor long ago. I still drink in his city. Neither is your business." }, { "The Brotherhood keeps a house at Thorium Point for strays, where they are kinder. Be a stray there first. If they ever learn your name, come back, and I will consider learning it too." }, { "Until then, away. Away." } },
    friendly = { title = "Terms", { "Thorium Point knows your name. So. Stand where I can see you, and hear the terms." }, { "We went down into the Fire Lord's halls once, for his cores and his leather and the blood of the mountain, which is his own tears. Many of us went down and did not come up again. Now you go. You are cheaper. Nothing personal. At TB Ltd., nothing ever is." }, { "Favor opens the Brotherhood's books, the plans and patterns nobody else in this world will sell you. It is the one coin I take that does not tarnish. Gold I can have from anyone." }, { "The offering is weighed. The offering is found sufficient. Do not let it go to your head." } },
    honored = { title = "The Small Knife", { "The Brotherhood receives you, and acknowledges your... oh, sit, if you like. Nobody sits with me. That is how you know it is an honor." }, { "You think we are Dark Irons who grew a conscience. Half of that is right. We were a guild before we were anything else, a craft guild in Ironforge, when there was one Ironforge and the clans had not yet gone to war over it. A frightened guild. We were sure our rivals knew secrets we did not. So we got hold of their best work and took it apart to see. That is how we found enchantment. Not by study. By theft, and patience, and a very small knife." }, { "When the war came and the clans chose sides, we chose. You know which. I will not apologize for it to a stranger, and I am still deciding what you are, so I will not apologize to you either." }, { "Our best secret, we stole first." } },
    revered = { title = "The Waste", { "The Brotherhood will hear your question. No. I will." }, { "You want to know why we left. Not the short version." }, { "When the Fire Lord woke, the mountain was his, and so were we. The emperor's people became his servants, and the Brotherhood became his smiths. We worked his forges. We made his weapons, the same blade over and over, for an army that did not care how well a thing was made. Understand me. It was not the cruelty. Dwarves can bear cruelty. It was the waste. The finest hands under the mountain, hammering out the same sword for creatures who could not tell it from a worse one." }, { "It was my apprentice who found the way out. Oilfist. Overseer Oilfist now, at Thorium Point, running the place like a garrison. He planned it under the overseers' noses, and we made what we needed to walk out of the Depths. Most who got free ran as far as their legs would carry them. We stopped across the Gorge. The materials are here. Craft does not run." }, { "And why am I here, at a table in the emperor's own city? The ale. Next question." } },
    aside = { title = "The aside", { "You again. Sit. No, not there. There. You have earned the better chair, which is the same chair, but I will know." } },
    exalted = { title = "Partners", { "No more ceremony. You and I are past weighing offerings. Listen, plainly, because this is the only way I talk to you now." }, { "The Brotherhood holds the secret of the Fire Lord's hammer. Sulfuras. The great maul he carries down there in the Core. We can teach a smith to forge the Sulfuron hammer, and with the Eye of Sulfuras set into it, a hero could carry the Hand of Ragnaros out into the world. Think about what that means. We spent an age making weapons for him. Now we sell the making of his own to anyone strong enough to kill him, at a fair price. I have never been so pleased with a piece of business in my life." }, { "I lose my head about it. Put a Sulfuron ingot in front of me and I will shout. I know. I do not care." }, { "Here is the other thing, since you are past the door. A guild like ours does not live on craft alone. When a rival grows too good, now and then, his forge has an accident. We are never anywhere near it. You will remember that we are never anywhere near it." }, { "You came to my table an insect. You leave it a partner. Read your contracts, all of them. Mine especially." } },
  },
}
-- (the places Classic Era's client names otherwise, swapped in there)
